course: dictionary
lesson: 16001
title: One word, two meanings: valerian
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can use the words around them to find out which meaning the writer wants. Valerian is one of these words. It can be a wild plant, or it can be a medicine made from that plant.
explain: «Mia picked a pink valerian flower beside the river.» Here valerian is a plant. The clues are picked, flower and river, which tell you it grows outdoors in a damp place.
explain: «Her grandma took a little valerian medicine to help her sleep.» Here valerian is a medicine. The clues are took, medicine and sleep. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "a little plant to help her sleep" make sense? Not really, so the medicine meaning fits better.
fact: Valerian is a tall wild plant with small, sweet-smelling pink or white flowers.
fact: Valerian grows by rivers and in damp places.
fact: Valerian is also a medicine made from the root of the plant.
fact: Some people take valerian medicine to help them sleep.
fact: Red valerian grows on old walls and cliffs in Britain.
exercise: «Mia picked a pink valerian flower beside the river.» What is valerian in this sentence? | *A tall wild plant with sweet-smelling flowers | A type of stone found on cliffs | A kind of bird with pink feathers | A fish that swims in rivers
exercise: «The cat rolled happily near the valerian root.» What part of the valerian plant is the cat near? | The leaves | The flowers | The seeds | *The root
exercise: Which place does valerian like to grow? | *Beside rivers and in damp places | Inside a house | On the top of mountains | A dry desert
test: «Her grandma took a little valerian medicine to help her sleep.» What is the medicine made from? | Pink flower petals | River water | *The root of the valerian plant | Sugar
test: Which sentence shows valerian as a plant? | *«The valerian smelled sweet on the riverbank.» | «She was very tired after school.» | «Grandma went to bed early.» | «The doctor gave her a tablet.»
exam: Which is a good way to decide whether valerian means the plant or the medicine? | Look only at the length of the word | Ignore the sentence and pick the first meaning you know | *Read the words around it and try each meaning in the sentence | Guess the meaning at random
